                <pb facs="0734" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857 Hannover/41: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Panama</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-14T16:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. Your 61, May 13, 1 p.m. Please ask Dr. Garay to delay any action concerning
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Hannover</hi> incident for two or three days pending
                    consideration by the Department of the question raised by Dr. Garay in the
                    telegram under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
